+## Context occupancy measurement
+
+The existing V4 Session usage projection owns optional `contextWindow.measurement`: source
+(`provider-usage`, `runtime-estimate`, `unknown`), state (`current`, `stale`), observation time,
+known request provider/model identity, and stale reason (`model-change`, `compaction`, `restored`).
+This is additive metadata, with no database migration or additional usage/Session store.
+
+Main ModelRequest identity → ModelComplete input-plus-output proxy → V4 snapshot/delta is the
+live path for desktop continuous delivery and remote snapshot/replay. Normalized cache and
+reasoning tokens are never added twice, and sidecars never replace occupancy. Cumulative
+consumption remains separate. Missing usage retains an old sample as stale instead of inventing
+a newly measured zero. A model switch invalidates the old sample, including a late completion
+for the previous request model; the configured capacity remains the newly selected model's.
+
+Only `truePostCompactTokenCount` establishes a post-compaction size, explicitly as a runtime
+estimate. Summary-request `postCompactTokenCount` is consumption, never occupancy. Successful
+compaction without a new size marks the previous sample stale. Existing durable assistant and
+compaction facts seed cold restoration; facts without measurement provenance are stale/restored.
+Completed main assistant metadata retains the existing estimated composition next to its own token
+usage. Cold restoration uses that active-branch message, not a new store or a nearby request's pie.
+Older messages without recorded composition stay unknown. Compaction discards unmatched composition.
+Legacy protocol payloads retain their shape while the V4 bridge carries the metadata. Synthetic
+tests cover main/sidecar calls, model switches, both compact outcomes, missing usage and restore.
+
+`usage.lastRequest` independently retains the latest main request's reported input, output,
+cache-read, cache-write and reasoning counts plus known request identity/time, even when capacity
+is unknown. Only finite nonnegative reports are included; a missing report replaces prior counts
+with an identity-only object. Reasoning is a subset of output, cache is a subset of normalized
+input, and neither is added again. Existing four cumulative buckets remain reported consumption.
+Cold restoration obtains lastRequest through the existing `queryTaskUsage` port from the latest
+`model_usage` main-turn row, ordered by completion/start time. Counters come only from normalized
+`raw_usage_json` fields; integer columns and legacy transcript zeros cannot prove a report. A newer
+error or missing-usage row supersedes older counters with identity/time only. The existing ledger
+and retention remain unchanged. The same query supplies cumulative raw main-turn counters from retained records, independent of context capacity, excluding sidecars and without the old statistics input-baseline subtraction. The label is recorded requests total, not an all-time invoice. Repeated or late seeds cannot overwrite a live main request. Optional/unavailable UsageStore support leaves the detail absent,
+and a delayed restore seed cannot replace any newer live main-request report.
