 ## Small context compaction
 
 Keep the existing output reservation and token accounting. The default safety buffer is the smaller of 13K and 10% of the effective input window, so a small but positive window does not compact after a few tokens. Explicit buffer values (including zero) retain precedence. The 200K/1M defaults, disabled state and failure circuit breaker retain their behavior. A zero effective input budget is still a separate unresolved request-budget boundary; no artificial positive threshold is created. `packages/core/test/compact-policy.test.ts` covers the bounded change.
